MTE is registered alongside DE and dispatches transfers synchronously, so I found no source-level blocker to observing its destination on the sibling’s stock configuration. The witness still needs care: a copy may appear correct if the PUT’s uninitialised tail happens to retain bytes from the preceding GET. The existing `rgb tiled64` row exercises DE, so it does not cover this MTE branch.
